question:
What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$x = 5;

function myFunction(){
    echo "Result $x";
}
myFunction();
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
function myFunction()
{
    $x = 5;
    echo "Result1: $x , ";
}
myFunction();
echo "Result2: $x";
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
function Increment(){
    static $num = 0;
    echo "$num";
    $num++;
}

Increment();
Increment();
Increment();
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$a = 5;
$b = 10;

print ("$a, $b+10");
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$value1 = NULL;
$value2 = null;

var_dump($value1);
var_dump($value2);
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$a = 123;
$b = "123";

var_dump($a !== $b);
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$a = 15;
$b = 20;

if ($a < ++$a || $b < ++$b){
    echo "True";
}
else{
    echo "False";
}
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$car = "Honda";

switch ($car) {
    case "Honda":
        echo "You selected Honda.";
    case "BMW":
        echo "You selected BMW.";
    case "AUDI":
        echo "You selected Audi.";
    default:
        echo "None is selected.";
}
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$counter = 1;

while ($counter++ <= 5)
{
    echo $counter, ",";
    $counter++;
}
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$cars = array(
    "BMW",
    "Mercedes",
    "Honda",
);

foreach ($cars as $c)
{
    echo "$c ";
}
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
for ($i = 1;$i <= 10;$i++){
    if ($i == 6){
        continue;
    }
    echo "$i ";
}
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$x = 10;

while ($x < 10) {
    $x++;
    echo $x, ",";
}
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php declare(strict_types = 1);

function details(string $name, int $age){
    echo "Name: $name, Age: $age";
}
details("Alvin", "21");
?>
```

explanation:
The syntax of defining a default argument value in PHP is:
function function_name(type $argument_name = value) { 
/* function body*/ 
}

The syntax of defining function return type in PHP is:
function function_name(type $arguments) : return_type { 
/* function body*/ 
}

question:
What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$str = "Hello, IncludeHelp";
$pattern = "/includehelp/i";

echo preg_match($pattern, $str);
?>
```

What will be the output of the following PHP code?
```
<?php
$str = "Hello, IncludeHelp";
$pattern = "/el/m";

echo preg_match($pattern, $str);
?>
```
